WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.308 --> 00:00:12.932
This lesson is for managers and founders. You will see how to watch your team on the Desk, add a new person, set up repeating work, and approve leave and expenses.

2
00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:32.429
Open the Desk every morning. Managers see their own team. Founders see everyone in the organisation. The tiles at the top show who needs attention, who to keep an eye on, who is on track, and how many stand-ups are in.

3
00:00:33.294 --> 00:00:48.990
Each person has a card with their overdue, blocked and open tasks, and when they last filed a stand-up. If someone is behind, click Nudge. It sends one friendly reminder, at most once a day.

4
00:00:49.857 --> 00:00:55.449
To add a new employee or intern, click People, then Add person.

5
00:00:57.625 --> 00:01:11.737
Type their name and their official email address. Choose their role, their department, their office, and who they report to. The reporting manager decides who approves their leave.

6
00:01:12.616 --> 00:01:24.112
Click Add person and send invite. They get the Welcome email straight away, and choose their own password. You never see or set it.

7
00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:34.848
For work that repeats, such as a weekly school visit, use Recurring. Click Recurring, then New recurring activity.

8
00:01:35.709 --> 00:01:54.021
Name the activity, choose how often it repeats, tick the days, and tick who it is for. Each person gets their own task and is scored separately. Click Create recurring activity, and KalamDesk creates each task for you at the right time.

9
00:01:54.875 --> 00:02:03.875
Next, leave. Click Leave. Requests from your team are listed under Waiting for your decision.

10
00:02:04.733 --> 00:02:16.109
Click Approve. You can hand over the person's open tasks to their cover person in one click. Or click Decline, and add a short note.

11
00:02:16.973 --> 00:02:35.453
Founders also approve expenses. Click Expenses. Open the receipt, then click Approve. Once you have paid, mark it paid. If you reject a claim, you must give a reason, and the employee sees it.

12
00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:54.754
Finally, the Dashboard. It shows completion trends, workload per person, overdue ageing, departments and top performers. Choose weekly or monthly, export to a spreadsheet, or publish a snapshot you can share.

13
00:02:55.618 --> 00:03:13.906
Under Incentives, set the rules once, and review awards on the first of every month. Under Templates, save the tasks you create again and again. And under Scores, the Scoring settings button lets you tune how points are worked out.

14
00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:25.268
That is how managers and founders run their teams in KalamDesk. The last lesson is for group owners who run more than one organisation.
